ADR-0015
title: E2E operator session re-entry for GUI verification
status: Accepted
date: 2026-08-16
decision_owner: Product owner
related:
  - docs/persistent-e2e-observation.md
  - backend/src/scripts/persistent-battle-e2e.ts
  - backend/src/e2e-observer.ts
  - v0.21.1 battle-screen deploy could not be exercised as a participant
authority: this file is the causal record; 0015-e2e-operator-session-reentry.md is the projection

PROBLEM P1
  GUI faults (bottom-nav crush, burger stacking, battlefield object dump,
  save-from-battle) take multiple releases to close because the operator
  cannot open the real BattlePage after Promote.
  Health and /internal/observations prove the API and the diagnostics
  screen. They do not prove scroll inset, accordion default, or the
  absence of persist controls.

EVIDENCE E1
  v0.21.1 shipped from unit tests plus production /api/health.
  BattlePage was not driven as a signed-in participant.
  Playwright exists on the operator machine but not in this workspace,
  and there is no login the browser can complete without Google OAuth.

EVIDENCE E2
  Persistent E2E already owns two non-human Supabase users
  (codex-e2e-observer@example.test kind=e2e,
   codex-e2e-opponent@example.test kind=test)
  and fixture characters, battlefield, and narrator.
  Each Observe job calls generateEphemeralPassword, writes it through
  the Supabase admin API, signs in once, and discards the secret.
  The password is not in secdat, the repo, or the observation artifact.

EVIDENCE E3
  0.8.0 made account_kind server-owned. Client claims cannot enter the
  test realm. General users must not see test-realm assets or ratings.
  /internal/observations is 404 for general users and is not BattlePage.

EVIDENCE E4
  ensurePersistentAccount already performs the only allowed password
  write for those identities. A second password store or a second auth
  provider would split that authority.

CAUSE C1
  The missing capability is not a browser binary. It is a way to obtain
  a short-lived, normal Supabase password session for an existing E2E
  identity after the operator is already authorized.

REJECTED O1: do nothing / Google-only Playwright
  Google OAuth is not a controllable E2E login. Leaving the gap keeps
  GUI verification as a manual afterthought.

REJECTED O2: stable password in secdat
  Contradicts the 0.8.0 rotation rule. A durable shared secret becomes
  a standing test-realm credential.

REJECTED O3: impersonation header or admin-acting-as
  BattlePage would render under the operator user id while pretending
  to be the fixture owner. That mixes identities, bypasses participant
  checks, and is a new privacy boundary.

REJECTED O4: new auth provider or session cookie that skips Supabase
  Production auth is Supabase JWKS. A parallel session type would fork
  user mapping and Stage/Promote smoke.

REJECTED O5: local legacy-auth Playwright only
  Useful for a screenshot. It does not exercise the promoted Worker,
  bottom-nav tokens, or production BattlePage.

DECISION O6: operator re-entry into the real E2E identity
  An already-authorized operator asks the server to rotate the fixture
  password the same way the Observe job does, receives the secret once,
  and signs in through the normal email/password path.
  After that, the browser session is the E2E user. BattlePage, history,
  and matchmaking run as that user. No impersonation.

OWNER_ACCEPTANCE
  Product owner accepted this revision of ADR-0015 on 2026-08-16 with
  the statement "受け入れます" after the Proposed text was presented.

ACCEPTANCE
  ADR-0015 revision dated 2026-08-16 is Accepted. Selected option is O6.
  Rules R1 through R10 are in force.

RULES
  R1. Reuse the existing fixture emails. Do not add a third human-looking
      account and do not change account_kind rules.
  R2. Mint is allowed only for a caller whose server-owned profile is
      admin or developer. general, test, and e2e callers get the same
      404 used by other internal routes. Client claims cannot opt in.
  R3. POST /api/internal/e2e-session with target observer | opponent
      rotates the password via generateEphemeralPassword and the
      existing Supabase admin write, then returns
      { email, password, accountKind } once. The secret is not stored.
  R4. The browser signs out the operator session and calls the normal
      Supabase password grant. There is no act-as header, no dual
      session, and no backend-issued cookie.
  R5. The same mint function may be called from a trusted runner
      (Playwright setup or Observe job). The runner already holds
      SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY. It must not print the password.
  R6. A mint invalidates the previous password. An in-flight Observe
      job that still holds a live access token may continue until that
      token expires; a later password grant by that job fails.
      Operators must not mint during a running Observe workflow.
  R7. Record a non-secret audit row (operator user id, target, time).
      Forbidden keys stay the same as observation sanitization:
      password, accessToken, auth/application ids in public artifacts.
  R8. UI: /internal/observations exposes re-entry only to
      admin/developer. The control names the target and states that
      the current session will end.
  R9. Playwright lives in this repository as the GUI verification
      tool. It logs in with a minted session and drives BattlePage.
      It is not a fifth required merge check. First use is operator
      and post-promote verification, not branch protection.
  R10. Playwright must exercise the usable viewport above the bottom
       navigation, the closed object accordion, and the absence of
       save-from-battle. API health is not a substitute.

CONSEQUENCES
  + Operator can open the same BattlePage a player sees, on staging
    or production, without Google in the automation path.
  + Password authority stays in one function.
  + Test-realm isolation is unchanged for general users.
  - Mint races the Observe job's next password grant.
  - The JSON response contains a secret for one hop.
  - Developer and admin can enter the fixture identities at will.

COMPATIBILITY
  No database migration. No change to users.account_kind, fixture
  ownership, or observation workflow confirmation.
  Application rollback does not need a schema undo.
  Existing Observe job remains the battle-pipeline observation path.

VERIFICATION after acceptance and implementation
  - general caller receives 404
  - admin/developer mint returns email+password; a second mint
    rejects the first password
  - sign-in with the returned password yields the fixture user's
    /api/me and accountKind
  - audit row exists and does not contain the password
  - Playwright opens BattlePage for a fixture battle and asserts
    R10 without using Google
